  "id": "conscious-moment",
  "term": "conscious moment",
  "definition": "A conscious moment is the intervening period in which consciousness weighs information from perceptual, motivational, cognitive, and emotional sources and produces will. In this view, that act of will then biases later neural activity toward carrying out the chosen goal.",
